<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Junnar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Junnar is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pune">Pune</a> district, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharashtra">Maharashtra</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, at the foot of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naneghat">Naneghat</a> pass. In the Satavahana and Kshaharata period it was a trading centre surrounded by more than two hundred rock-cut Buddhist caves, among the largest groups in India. The nearby hill fort of Shivneri was the birthplace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/junnar.jpg" alt="Junnar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elroy Serrao · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Junnar_city.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
